steal. They have daily lunch special which is reasonably price and are delectable. Today I had the chicken drumettes plate looking at another patron's plate I'm glad I ordered it 10pcs with fries $10. My cousin opted for the grilled chicken salad which looked like tomorrow's lunch."},{"business_id":"9MdAr_MK8YUzYsEHMf1QeA","review_id":"xe_pEt8T6ZzsPUQwxPrctA","date":"2016-04-22T19:01:03","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9135717153549194,"text_excerpt":"I was very impressed! The food was great and the ambiance was just perfect. I had the spinach and artichoke dip (which was awesome) and the steak as my entrée. I'm very impressed. On another note-I'm not from the area and had a hard time finding it because there wasn't signage, so my only request is to put something up - I'm sure it will bring more business. I drove up and down the street for a few minutes and took a chance before just leaving to go into the Bartholomew golf center and there it was."},{"business_id":"9MdAr_MK8YUzYsEHMf1QeA","review_id":"XK76uTkXI6TC8iWipDo2Nw","date":"2015-10-21T05:08:03","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.904227077960968,"text_excerpt":"Great location, Great food!! I visited Lenora's this past weekend for some lunch and was very pleased. I'm a Gumbo junkie/critic and will try just about any gumbo from a restaurant . The gumbo at Lenora's is home cooked gumbo with fresh shrimp crab and has a nice kick. Spin and Art dip was also very good and tasty. Fried Oysters were a nice golden brown gulf oyster served on a fresh French bread Excellent service, definitely will return . This is one spot you won't want to miss out on."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
